blockspec is licensed per directory, on the same split as rowspec. This is
deliberate, not an oversight.

  SPEC.md, docs/            CC-BY-4.0
  conformance/cases/        CC0-1.0
  conformance/*.py          MIT
  reference/, tests/        Apache-2.0 OR MIT
  spike/*.md                CC-BY-4.0
  spike/harness/*           MIT
  spike/harness/plant_cases/  CC0-1.0

Full texts are in LICENSES/.

WHY THE SPLIT

The point of this project is independent implementations. That makes the
reusability of the SPEC and the FIXTURES more important than the licence on any
reference code.

CommonMark embeds its conformance examples inside a CC-BY-SA spec document, so
vendoring the test cases arguably vendors share-alike prose. These fixtures are
meant to be vendored: copy them into an implementation in any language, under
any licence, without obligation.

NOTHING IS LICENSED YET BECAUSE NOTHING EXISTS YET. This file is here so the
split is decided before the first file lands, rather than retrofitted after.
